{"id": "striviaqa0133", "pool": "striviaqa", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 11, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Before adopting the U.S. dollar in the early 2000s, Ecuador used a currency called the e cuadorian su reño, often just referred to as the su reño. It was officially known as the su reño because it was pegged to gold at a fixed rate, reflecting its historical link to the Spanish colon ial monetary system. The sureño was divided into 10 0 centavos and circulated from the mid-1 9 60 s until E cuador switched to the U.S. dollar on January 1, 20 00, as part of an economic stabilization plan.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 32, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "striviaqa0141", "pool": "striviaqa", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The A23 road connects London to the coastal resort of B righton in East Sussex.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
